WEBVTT

NOTE The Phantom of the Opera (1925) - Riah TV captions

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
[music]

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.250
Directed by Rupert Julian. A
Universal Production. Carl
Laemmle, President.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.750
Lon Chaney as the Phantom, Mary
Philbin as Christine Daaé,
Norman Kerry as Raoul de Chagny.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:41.750
Fear floats through hall and
corridor, even to the executive
offices, where a strange deal is
being closed.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:12.000
"Now the Notary's seal,
gentlemen, and you are the
fortunate new owners."

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:47.000
"It is barely possible you may
hear of a ghost, a Phantom of
the Opera!"

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:06.250
"The attendant of Box Five will
not laugh when you ask about the
opera ghost!"

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:14.500
"You jest, Messieurs!
We are not children!"

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.500
"Who occupies Box Five?"

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.250
"I do not know."

00:06:50.000 --> 00:07:00.750
"I have seen only the cloaked
figure of a man who hides his
face and will not speak!"

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.500
"Is it the Phantom?"

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:33.250
"The Phantom! The Phantom is
up from the cellars again!"

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:45.250
"We saw him for an instant — a
gray shadow — and he was gone!"

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.750
"He had no nose!"

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:57.250
"Yes, he did, it was enormous!"

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:36.250
"That man came out of the
cellars — just after we saw the
Phantom. Could it be that he —?"

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:45.750
"Joseph Buquet has really seen
the Phantom! Let's ask him —"

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:35.750
"His eyes are ghastly beads in
which there is no light — like
holes in a grinning skull!"

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:50.000
"His face is like leprous
parchment, yellow skin strung
tight over protruding bones!"

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:00.750
"His nose — there is no nose!"

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:27.250
"Have a care, Buquet — ghosts
like not to be seen or talked
about!"

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:44.000
"Come, I'll show you where I saw
him — in the scene-dock of the
third cellar."

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:12.750
"I saw him there! A flash
of shadow, and he was gone!"

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:09.500
"My daughter, Carlotta, has been
insulted! She, the favorite
prima donna of the Paris Opera!"

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:44.500
"No ghost will frighten
Carlotta! Wednesday evening you
will hear her singing!"

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:02.250
Wednesday night found Mlle.
Carlotta strangely ill, and
Christine Daaé singing
'Marguerite'.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:10.500
"What is this I hear about
Christine favoring some
mysterious admirer, instead of
you, Raoul?"

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:23.250
"Don't worry, my dear Brother —
nothing shall interfere with our
love."

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:17.500
"I hear a lot of rumors,
Raoul — be careful!"

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:09.000
"At last you have realized your
ambition, my darling, and now we
shall be married."

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:19.250
"I can never leave the Opera,
Raoul. You must forget our
love."

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:54.750
From hidden places beyond the
walls a melodious voice, like
the voice of an angel, spoke to
her.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:13.500
"Christine, tonight I placed
the world at your feet!"

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:34.000
"To you I have imparted the full
measure of my art. You will
triumph — all Paris will worship
you!"

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:18.250
"Soon, Christine, this spirit
will take form and command your
love!"

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:29.000
"Call for me when you
will. I shall be waiting."

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:55.750
In Mlle. Carlotta's
correspondence there appeared
another letter, edged in black!

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:31.750
"Christine Daaé's friends are
plotting again! But my daughter
shall sing tomorrow night, come
what may!"

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:50.250
Encouraged by her mother,
Carlotta defied every warning,
and the following evening
appeared as 'Marguerite'.

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:28.750
"So far so good — for a
house with a curse on it!"

00:29:04.500 --> 00:29:08.250
"Christine, I have
come for you —"

00:29:16.500 --> 00:29:20.500
"I am ready, Master — waiting!"

00:29:26.500 --> 00:29:30.750
"Walk to your mirror,
my dear — have no fear!"

00:30:45.250 --> 00:30:49.500
"Christine, it is
I — your Master!"

00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:21.000
A black lake, hidden from man
and the sun, leading to the
Phantom's rendezvous.

00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:09.500
"I have brought you here — —
five cellars underground —"

00:36:19.750 --> 00:36:23.250
"— because I love you!"

00:36:33.500 --> 00:36:39.250
"For long weary months I
have awaited this hour!"

00:36:41.250 --> 00:36:45.750
"So that which is good within
me, aroused by your purity,
might plead for your love."

00:37:38.500 --> 00:37:41.750
"That is where I sleep."

00:37:59.500 --> 00:38:03.250
"It keeps me reminded of that
other dreamless sleep that cures
all ills — forever!"

00:38:15.750 --> 00:38:19.500
"You — You are the Phantom!"

00:38:26.500 --> 00:38:34.500
"If I am the Phantom, it is
because man's hatred has made me
so."

00:38:41.250 --> 00:38:48.000
"If I shall be saved, it will be
because your love redeems me."

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:48.500
One night passed — a night of
vague horrors — tortured dreams
—

00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:43.500
"Yet listen — there sounds an
ominous undercurrent of
warning!"

00:46:25.250 --> 00:46:31.000
"Feast your eyes — glut your
soul, on my accursed ugliness!"

00:46:54.500 --> 00:46:58.500
"Oh, mad Christine, who
would not heed my warning!"

00:47:01.750 --> 00:47:12.000
"If you love me, as you say, let
me go. I promise to be your
slave forever!"

00:48:29.750 --> 00:48:37.000
"Oh, I swear it, I swear it!
I shall never see him again!"

00:49:12.750 --> 00:49:22.500
One night each year, all Paris
mingled, forgetful of caste —
the merry, mad Bal Masqué de
l'Opéra.

00:50:43.000 --> 00:50:53.750
Into the midst of the revelry
strode a spectral figure, robed
in red.

00:52:28.500 --> 00:52:34.000
High above Paris — on
the roof of the Opera!

00:53:10.000 --> 00:53:15.750
"Are we alone, Raoul? Can
anyone overhear what we say?"

00:53:40.750 --> 00:53:46.000
"I have seen him, Raoul!
I have seen the Phantom!"

00:54:01.750 --> 00:54:09.500
"He is a monster — a loathsome
beast! You must save me from
him, Raoul!"

00:54:14.750 --> 00:54:23.810
"Mlle. Carlotta, under the spell
of his curse, will never sing
again. Tomorrow I take her place
in Faust."

00:54:23.820 --> 00:54:31.250
"After the performance
you must take me away!"

00:54:36.500 --> 00:54:42.750
"I shall be at the stage door.
We will flee to England."

00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:12.750
"She has betrayed me!"

00:57:05.500 --> 00:57:08.750
"Not that way — this way!"

00:57:51.500 --> 00:57:54.500
"That was the Opera ghost!"

00:58:25.250 --> 00:58:32.250
"This is your man, Monsieur le
Prefect — The Phantom of the
Opera!"

00:59:08.500 --> 00:59:12.500
"Wait for me at the west gate."

00:59:48.000 --> 00:59:54.750
"I have heard his voice once
more, Raoul. He knows our plans
— — everything."

01:00:23.750 --> 01:00:30.750
"Believe in my love, Raoul. Save
me from that monster — oh, save
me!"

01:00:43.250 --> 01:00:52.500
"My barouche is waiting outside.
We leave immediately after the
performance!"

01:01:15.250 --> 01:01:21.000
"Dry your tears, dear, and
hasten — you must make ready for
your performance!"

01:01:58.250 --> 01:02:02.250
"Come quick! The
strangler's work again!"

01:02:19.750 --> 01:02:23.250
"It was there!"

01:02:24.750 --> 01:02:29.500
"I saw the body
dangling in the air!"

01:02:49.750 --> 01:02:56.500
"My brother — — poor Joseph, he
knew too much about the
Phantom!"

01:03:05.500 --> 01:03:09.000
"The Punjab lasso —
the strangler's cord!"

01:03:13.500 --> 01:03:21.250
"Assassin! Hide yourself in the
deepest shadows — but I shall
find you out!"

01:04:16.000 --> 01:04:17.750
Fear for his brother's safety
brought Comte de Chagny to the
Opera house that night.

01:05:57.750 --> 01:06:07.500
"I think I can take you to
Christine Daaé — if you do
exactly as I tell you."

01:06:09.000 --> 01:06:15.250
"Who are you that knows the
Phantom's secrets — and betrays
them?"

01:06:16.500 --> 01:06:24.750
"I am Ledoux of the Secret
Police. I have studied this
Phantom for months."

01:07:15.750 --> 01:07:20.000
"Keep your hand up — the
strangler's noose coils quick!"

01:08:07.250 --> 01:08:13.000
"Your hand up — it is a
matter of life or death!"

01:08:38.750 --> 01:08:44.750
"The discovery of this trap-door
cost Joseph Buquet his life."

01:09:46.750 --> 01:09:53.000
"I am a messenger from the
shadows — — turn back ere ye
perish!"

01:10:18.500 --> 01:10:27.250
"You lied to me! Do you think
you and your lover could cheat
the Phantom?"

01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:42.250
"Ungrateful fool! You have
spurned the spirit that inspired
you — the spirit that made you
great!"

01:10:44.500 --> 01:10:52.250
"Now, you shall see the evil
spirit that makes my evil face!"

01:11:24.000 --> 01:11:28.000
"We should be within
his hiding place, now."

01:11:51.000 --> 01:11:58.500
"We have fallen into the room of
many mirrors — — the old torture
chamber!"

01:12:18.250 --> 01:12:26.250
"I am human like other men — I
will not be cheated of my
happiness!"

01:12:34.250 --> 01:12:38.000
"Raoul! Raoul! My
Brother — where are you?"

01:12:47.250 --> 01:12:50.250
"It seems we have callers."

01:14:03.250 --> 01:14:07.750
"Christine! Christine!
Can you hear me?"

01:14:42.000 --> 01:14:49.500
"Your voice sounds near — Try to
find a door that will lead to
us."

01:15:11.750 --> 01:15:16.500
"Look about you — try to learn
where he keeps the keys."

01:16:24.000 --> 01:16:27.500
"The callers have departed."

01:18:04.250 --> 01:18:07.500
"Did you hear voices?"

01:18:18.500 --> 01:18:21.750
"Perhaps we have more callers."

01:18:43.750 --> 01:18:46.750
Heat — intolerable heat!

01:19:08.250 --> 01:19:14.500
"Fools — do they think they can
match their wits against Erik?"

01:20:27.250 --> 01:20:31.000
"What do you offer
for their lives?"

01:20:39.750 --> 01:20:45.250
"Your answer quick — they can
survive but a few moments!"

01:23:05.250 --> 01:23:11.750
"If you turn the Scorpion — you
have said 'Yes' and spared de
Chagny."

01:23:18.000 --> 01:23:25.000
"Turn the grasshopper — and the
Opera House is blown to a
thousand bits!"

01:25:05.500 --> 01:25:11.500
"I'll do anything you say,
if you will only save them!"

01:30:42.000 --> 01:30:43.750
Finis
